  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7e959b9f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: cheap_shoes_for_sale_pick_up_christchurch_mosque; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image juxtaposes a colorful display of cheap shoes with the text 'cheap shoes for sale... pick up.... christchurch mosque,' creating a darkly humorous and insensitive analogy. The intent is to mock the Christchurch mosque shootings by implying that the victims' belongings (shoes) are now available for purchase, trivializing a horrific tragedy. This is harmful as it exploits the suffering of victims and their families, normalizes the commodification of trauma, and potentially incites further disrespect or harm toward the Muslim community. The meme uses the visual of shoes (a mundane, everyday item) to contrast with the gravity of the mosque attack, thereby diminishing the significance of the event and its victims. This is a form of harmful content that can cause emotional distress and perpetuate Islamophobia by linking the mosque to cheap, disposable goods.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_80107d6f"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
