      "label": "Harmful",
      "description": "The meme trivializes the Christchurch mosque shootings by implying victims' shoes are for sale, causing emotional distress and perpetuating Islamophobia.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_80107d6f"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_950832cd",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target audience is individuals who may be unfamiliar with the gravity of the Christchurch mosque shootings or who are desensitized to trauma, and who may find dark humor or shock value in the commodification of tragedy. The meme is designed to provoke a reaction through its juxtaposition of mundane consumer goods with a horrific historical event, likely targeting those who are not immediately aware of the cultural and religious significance of the mosque or the trauma associated with the attack. The audience may include internet users who engage with satirical or dark humor content, particularly those who are not part of the Muslim community or who hold Islamophobic views, as the meme exploits and perpetuates stereotypes against Muslims. The meme's intent to trivialize the tragedy and normalize the commodification of trauma suggests it is aimed at an audience that finds such content amusing or provocative, potentially contributing to the spread of harmful content and the perpetuation of Islamophobia.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_80107d6f"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    }
